silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_02_typed_noun_discipline_sections_02_domestic_cat_anchor_typed_concrete_anchor_4_tau_N#typednoungate silm:hasLongDescription "The TypedNounGate is the typing gate applied to 'a domestic cat'. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'tau_N', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
